Read health, environmental and equipment requirements (@wu-requirements: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @water-and-sanitation, #source "../sources/Potabilidade-e-Vigilancia-Vigiagua.lingua#r_0MJJ4WY69D303TQ11X6TNZZ779", #source "../sources/Drinking-Water-Quality-WHO-2026.lingua#r_71BB45J2CZ76C0WZ6H1C7SWZ5F", #source "../sources/Industrial-Water-Treatment-UFC-3-230-13.lingua#r_41KNKBCA6GZWQ6VAJGAPG2HJ3R", #water-and-sanitation "../../../../inquiry/metrology/foundations/Sampling-and-representativeness.lingua#r_0F0VEC42GPQPRZM0S7MXF7GAEH") { r_20CZ4H0Z5Z92MH7VM5ED5K54J5
**Read:** [Potabilidade e vigilância da água — Ministério da Saúde](../sources/Potabilidade-e-Vigilancia-Vigiagua.lingua#r_0MJJ4WY69D303TQ11X6TNZZ779), the official index and applicable consolidated provisions; [Guidelines for drinking-water quality — WHO, 2026 consolidated edition](../sources/Drinking-Water-Quality-WHO-2026.lingua#r_71BB45J2CZ76C0WZ6H1C7SWZ5F), chapters 2–5; [Industrial Water Treatment Operation and Maintenance — UFC 3-230-13](../sources/Industrial-Water-Treatment-UFC-3-230-13.lingua#r_41KNKBCA6GZWQ6VAJGAPG2HJ3R), applicability and equipment-specific treatment criteria.

A design needs requirements with an identified authority and scope. Drinking-water health protection, discharge permissions, receiving-water objectives, reuse conditions and equipment-quality specifications apply at different boundaries. A universal list of numbers would hide those differences.

For a selected requirement, record the jurisdiction or contract, applicable edition, system category, constituent and reporting basis, sampling location, averaging or compliance rule and action required after a failure. Read definitions and exceptions with the numerical table. Compare a current requirement with the date and purpose of an older technical manual.

Use [Potabilidade e vigilância da água — Ministério da Saúde](../sources/Potabilidade-e-Vigilancia-Vigiagua.lingua#r_0MJJ4WY69D303TQ11X6TNZZ779) for the Brazilian drinking-water framework and [Guidelines for drinking-water quality — WHO, 2026 consolidated edition](../sources/Drinking-Water-Quality-WHO-2026.lingua#r_71BB45J2CZ76C0WZ6H1C7SWZ5F) for its international scientific context. Determine separately the relevant environmental authority and the destination's conditions for wastewater or residuals. An educational model can explain a concentration or pressure; only the applicable evidence and assessment can establish compliance for the real service.

